{"beat": 31, "name": "THE EDGES", "text": "And the card had edges, and the edges decided who won. On August 15, 1913, the post office changed the card. Zones 1 and 2 were merged at 5 cents, plus 1 cent a pound, because, the official in charge explained, 30% of all shipments went to those zones. On January 1, 1914, the weight limit nearby rose to 50 pounds. And then a congressional committee found the town of Bavaria, Kansas. A 50-pound parcel to Bavaria cost 54 cents from a mail-order house in Kansas City, 193 miles away by rail. From a merchant in Salina, 7 miles away, it cost the same. The committee's word for it was inequitable. And notice who could fix it. Congress had done something unusual in the Act: it let the Postmaster General change the rates, the zones and the weights himself, with the consent of the Interstate Commerce Commission. The card could be redrawn without a new law. It was, again and again.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "And", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.18}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.18, "end": 0.26}, {"word": "card", "start": 0.26, "end": 0.56}, {"word": "had", "start": 0.56, "end": 0.8}, {"word": "edges,", "start": 0.8, "end": 1.22}, {"word": "and", "start": 1.64, "end": 1.8}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.8, "end": 1.92}, {"word": "edges", "start": 1.92, "end": 2.26}, {"word": "decided", "start": 2.26, "end": 2.86}, {"word": "who", "start": 2.86, "end": 3.1}, {"word": "won.", "start": 3.1, "end": 3.46}, {"word": "On", "start": 4.1, "end": 4.26}, {"word": "August", "start": 4.26, "end": 4.56}, {"word": "15,", "start": 4.56, "end": 5.06}, {"word": "1913,", "start": 5.34, "end": 6.26}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.04, "end": 7.1}, {"word": "post", "start": 7.1, "end": 7.36}, {"word": "office", "start": 7.36, "end": 7.76}, {"word": "changed", "start": 7.76, "end": 8.14}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.14, "end": 8.38}, {"word": "card.", "start": 8.38, "end": 8.72}, {"word": "Zones", "start": 9.46, "end": 9.76}, {"word": "1", "start": 9.76,